WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.923
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, it’s 9:01, let’s get started. Hope everyone’s doing well. Quick round of updates before we dive in?</v>

00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:20.008
<v Lukas Brenner>Sure, I can go first. Not much from EMEA this week, just a couple of travel insurance questions from the Paris team, but nothing urgent.</v>

00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:31.646
<v Priya Raman>APAC’s been pretty quiet too. I did get a ping about the ISOS app from someone in Singapore, but I think it was just a download issue.</v>

00:00:32.992 --> 00:00:40.684
<v Daniel Ferreira>Comp side is all good. I’m still working on the salary benchmarking refresh, but that’s not due until next month.</v>

00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:50.147
<v Tomás Rivera>Legal’s all clear. I did review the travel policy language you sent, Maya, and I have a couple of minor notes, but nothing blocking.</v>

00:00:51.305 --> 00:01:01.689
<v Maya Okafor>Great, thanks everyone. I’ll just add that I’m prepping for the Q3 benefits review, so if you have anything you want flagged, let me know by Friday.</v>

00:01:02.321 --> 00:01:03.821
<v Lukas Brenner>Will do, Maya.</v>

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:09.462
<v Priya Raman>Same here, I’ll send you a note if anything pops up.</v>

00:01:10.705 --> 00:01:20.320
<v Maya Okafor>Awesome. Okay, main agenda: the handbook update for the Business Travel Emergency Assistance & Accident Policy. You all saw the draft in the doc, right?</v>

00:01:21.644 --> 00:01:29.721
<v Daniel Ferreira>Yep, I read through it. The structure looks good to me, and I like that we’re keeping the ISOS instructions clear.</v>

00:01:30.975 --> 00:01:38.667
<v Lukas Brenner>Agreed. I think the new version is a bit easier to follow, especially with the app download steps up top.</v>

00:01:39.214 --> 00:01:49.598
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I like that too. I did wonder if we should clarify that the coverage is for both domestic and international travel, just so it’s super explicit.</v>

00:01:50.822 --> 00:02:00.053
<v Maya Okafor>Good point, Priya. I think the intro paragraph says it, but maybe we can bold it or call it out in the details section?</v>

00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:10.778
<v Tomás Rivera>I’d support that. Sometimes people skim and miss the intro. Maybe just add a bullet under 'Coverage' that says 'applies to both domestic and international business travel'.</v>

00:02:12.112 --> 00:02:14.419
<v Lukas Brenner>I can add that, no problem.</v>

00:02:15.736 --> 00:02:21.889
<v Daniel Ferreira>One thing—do we need to mention anything about dependents? I know we get that question sometimes.</v>

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:29.302
<v Maya Okafor>Right, but I think the policy is still just for employees, not family members. Tomás, is that correct?</v>

00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:40.179
<v Tomás Rivera>That’s right. The ISOS coverage is only for team members traveling on company business. We can add a line to clarify that if you want.</v>

00:02:40.977 --> 00:02:46.362
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, maybe just a quick note so people don’t assume their spouse is covered.</v>

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:52.343
<v Lukas Brenner>I’ll add a sentence under 'Coverage'—something like, 'Coverage applies to employees only, not dependents.'</v>

00:02:53.577 --> 00:02:55.077
<v Maya Okafor>Perfect. Anything else?</v>

00:02:55.573 --> 00:02:57.496
<v Daniel Ferreira>Nope, that covers my questions.</v>

00:02:57.727 --> 00:02:59.265
<v Priya Raman>All good from me.</v>

00:02:59.716 --> 00:03:01.216
<v Tomás Rivera>Same here.</v>

00:03:01.843 --> 00:03:14.151
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, so to recap: we’re updating the handbook page to clarify that coverage is for both domestic and international business travel, and that it’s for employees only. Lukas, you’ll make those edits?</v>

00:03:15.474 --> 00:03:22.397
<v Lukas Brenner>Yep, I’ll update the page and ping you all for review. Should have it done by next Friday.</v>

00:03:23.854 --> 00:03:29.623
<v Maya Okafor>Thanks, Lukas. Once it’s live, I’ll post in #travel-support so folks know about the update.</v>

00:03:30.186 --> 00:03:31.686
<v Priya Raman>Great, thanks Maya.</v>

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.220
<v Daniel Ferreira>Sounds good.</v>

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.440
<v Tomás Rivera>Works for me.</v>

00:03:37.915 --> 00:03:50.223
<v Maya Okafor>Okay, last agenda item—quick one. We got the results from the annual benefits satisfaction survey. Overall scores are up, but there were a few comments about the travel insurance process being confusing.</v>

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:58.428
<v Lukas Brenner>That tracks with some of the questions I’ve been getting. Maybe we need a short FAQ or a one-pager?</v>

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:04.080
<v Priya Raman>I like that idea. Even just a simple flowchart could help.</v>

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.430
<v Daniel Ferreira>Yeah, something visual would be good. People don’t always read the full policy.</v>

00:04:10.891 --> 00:04:22.430
<v Maya Okafor>Okay, let’s do this: Lukas, can you draft a one-pager or FAQ for the travel insurance process? Doesn’t have to be fancy, just something we can link from the handbook.</v>

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:27.477
<v Lukas Brenner>Sure, I’ll put something together and share a draft by the 10th.</v>

00:04:28.928 --> 00:04:30.428
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Lukas!</v>

00:04:30.973 --> 00:04:32.473
<v Tomás Rivera>Appreciate it.</v>

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.314
<v Daniel Ferreira>Thanks, Lukas.</v>

00:04:35.079 --> 00:04:39.310
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, that’s everything on the agenda. Anything else before we wrap?</v>

00:04:40.457 --> 00:04:41.957
<v Priya Raman>Nothing from me.</v>

00:04:42.565 --> 00:04:44.065
<v Lukas Brenner>All good here.</v>

00:04:45.053 --> 00:04:46.553
<v Daniel Ferreira>Nope, I’m good.</v>

00:04:47.418 --> 00:04:48.918
<v Tomás Rivera>I’m all set.</v>

00:04:49.619 --> 00:04:57.696
<v Maya Okafor>Okay, thanks everyone. Lukas, let us know if you have any questions on the edits. Otherwise, see you all next week!</v>

00:04:58.645 --> 00:05:02.491
<v Lukas Brenner>Will do. Have a good rest of your week, everyone.</v>

00:05:03.022 --> 00:05:04.522
<v Priya Raman>Bye all!</v>

00:05:05.644 --> 00:05:07.144
<v Daniel Ferreira>Take care.</v>

00:05:07.346 --> 00:05:08.846
<v Tomás Rivera>Bye!</v>

00:05:10.249 --> 00:05:11.749
<v Maya Okafor>Bye!</v>
